0..72 Comment "//! Freshness conditions on rules [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting] and"
73..150 Comment "//! [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]. A rule between"
151..231 Comment "//! terms closes on a `where` clause, `where a # q`: the atom `a` stands outside"
232..311 Comment "//! the support of the term `q` stands for. A rule whose variable moves into or"
312..387 Comment "//! out of an abstraction states that atom fresh for it, or the description"
388..465 Comment "//! check refuses the rule for capture (`pathological/desc/freshness.gandr`)."
466..546 Comment "//! The value of `Theory` keeps each condition as a `Fresh` link after its rule."
547..625 Comment "//! No port of these theories takes an atom, so no term names one: the support"
626..705 Comment "//! of every instance is empty and every condition holds. Where a port takes an"
706..757 Comment "//! atom, a condition decides where its rule fires:"
758..797 Comment "//! `model/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr`."
798..801 Comment "//!"
802..849 Comment "//! - cites: [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]"
850..920 Comment "//! - cites: [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]"
921..924 Comment "//!"
925..1048 Comment "//! [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2006.12.002 \"Fernández and Gabbay, Nominal rewriting\""
1049..1214 Comment "//! [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]: https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139084673 \"Pitts, Nominal Sets: Names and Symmetry in Computer Science\""
1216..1288 Comment "/// The π-calculus\'s structural congruence: the inert process, parallel"
1289..1358 Comment "/// composition and restriction, scope extrusion moving `q` under the"
1359..1437 Comment "/// restriction fresh for its atom. The checker orients the law and the kernel"
1438..1462 Comment "/// replays the verdict."
